-- title:
--   Nodal geometric special fibre of X₁(Mp), chartwise
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field $L((q))$ generated by the image, under coefficientwise application of $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$ in $L$; assume $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $L((q))$ the coefficientwise base change of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\,$`jNumQ` of the modular invariant. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ that is an $A$-algebra. Write $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $A_{\mathrm{inf}}$ for the subalgebras of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, respectively over $A[j^{-1}]$ (the project's `chartAlgFin` and `chartAlgInf`). Then, for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak{M}$ of $k \otimes_A A_{\mathrm{fin}}$, and likewise for every maximal ideal of $k \otimes_A A_{\mathrm{inf}}$, there exist $u, v$ in the localisation at $\mathfrak{M}$ with $u v = 0$ and with the maximal ideal of that localisation equal to the ideal generated by $u$ and $v$.
--
--   The two tensor products are the coordinate rings of the two affine charts of the geometric special fibre at $p$ of the integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$ built from the integral closures of $A[j]$ and $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$; the conclusion is the ring-theoretic form of the assertion that each closed point of this fibre is either smooth (take $u = 0$ and $v$ a uniformiser) or an ordinary double point, as in the theory of stable models with $\Gamma_1(p)$-structure. It is used to show that the relevant localisations of the rings obtained by adjoining Gauss reductions to these charts are discrete valuation rings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_mul_eq_zero_and_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair_localization_tensor_chartAlg_x1_mul.lean

